window.MC_WIKI = {"pages":[{"slug":"index","title":"MeshCrowd Wiki","desc":"Guides and reference for installing, using, running and extending MeshCrowd. Start with Getting started, or search above.","group":"Start here","headings":[{"id":"conventions","text":"Conventions","level":2}],"text":" Welcome to the MeshCrowd wiki. It explains how to set up a server, how every feature works and how to run a community with it. Press / anywhere on this page to search. note Where to begin New here? Read Getting started getting started.html for a ten minute tour, then Installation installation.html if you are about to host a server. If you only want to join someone else's community, Clients clients.html is all you need. {{index}} Conventions A name in code is something you type, click or find in a file. Manage Server , Manage Roles and similar are permissions a role can carry. The server owner always has all of them. Paths such as data/config.json are relative to the folder that contains the server. "},{"slug":"getting-started","title":"Getting started","desc":"A ten-minute tour: start a server, create an account, make your first server and invite someone.","group":"Start here","headings":[{"id":"what-you-need","text":"What you need","level":2},{"id":"1-start-the-server","text":"1. Start the server","level":2},{"id":"2-open-it-and-create-the-owner-account","text":"2. Open it and create the owner account","level":2},{"id":"3-create-your-first-server","text":"3. Create your first server","level":2},{"id":"4-invite-people","text":"4. Invite people","level":2},{"id":"5-add-a-voice-channel","text":"5. Add a voice channel","level":2},{"id":"6-pick-your-clients","text":"6. Pick your clients","level":2},{"id":"where-to-go-next","text":"Where to go next","level":2}],"text":" This page takes you from nothing to a running community. Every step links to a deeper page. What you need A computer that stays on while people use it a spare PC, a small server or a rented VPS. On Windows, nothing else. The server bundle carries its own Node.js. On Linux and macOS, install Node.js 22.5 or newer . A modern browser. 1. Start the server On Windows, unzip the server bundle and double click start server.bat . On Linux or macOS The first start creates a data/ folder with the database, a configuration file and a self signed certificate. See Installation installation.html for the portable bundle and updates. 2. Open it and create the owner account Open https //localhost 8443 and accept the certificate warning once. The warning is expected the certificate was generated by your own server. Register an account. The first account becomes the Owner with full administrator rights. The chat view after signing in ../assets/img/chat general.jpg 3. Create your first server Click the green + in the left rail and choose Create server . Give it a name. You get a general text channel to begin with. Use the + next to Channels to add more, and the server name at the top to open Server Settings . note Start from a template If someone shared a template code with you, paste it into the Template code field when creating the server to start from their structure. See Community tools community tools.html . 4. Invite people Open Server Settings, Invites , create an invite and send the link Copy link gives an address like https //192.168.1.10 8443/i/<code that opens a join page; the plain code still works in the Join tab . People on the same network can use your LAN address. For people outside your network you will want a domain name and a proper certificate see TLS and reverse proxies tls.html . warn Set publicHost first If other devices will connect, set publicHost in data/config.json to the address people will type before the first start, so the certificate is issued for it. Changing it later means deleting data/certs/ and restarting. 5. Add a voice channel Create a channel of type Voice . Pick a quality preset now it is fixed once the channel exists. Join from the sidebar and allow microphone access. Calls need HTTPS or localhost . See Voice, video and stages voice video.html . 6. Pick your clients Browser nothing to install. Desktop app a portable Windows client. See Clients clients.html . Android see the Android app android.html guide. Where to go next Learn how permissions work in Servers, channels and roles servers channels.html . Protect your community with Moderation and safety moderation.html . Automate things with Bots, API and webhooks bots api.html . Back up with a single folder copy Administration administration.html . "},{"slug":"installation","title":"Installation and updates","desc":"Requirements, the portable bundle, running from source, ports, backups and how to update.","group":"Start here","headings":[{"id":"requirements","text":"Requirements","level":2},{"id":"windows-the-portable-bundle","text":"Windows: the portable bundle","level":2},{"id":"linux-and-macos-from-source","text":"Linux and macOS: from source","level":2},{"id":"what-the-first-start-creates","text":"What the first start creates","level":2},{"id":"ports","text":"Ports","level":2},{"id":"running-as-a-service","text":"Running as a service","level":2},{"id":"backups","text":"Backups","level":2},{"id":"updating","text":"Updating","level":2},{"id":"building-the-portable-bundle-yourself","text":"Building the portable bundle yourself","level":2}],"text":" Requirements Part Needs Server Node.js 22.5 or newer it uses the built in node sqlite module . A suitable node.exe is bundled on Windows. Memory and disk A few hundred MB of RAM for a small community, and enough disk for uploads. Browser A current Chromium, Firefox or Safari based browser. Voice and video HTTPS or localhost , plus the built in STUN/TURN server or an external one for people on different networks. See STUN and TURN configuration.html stun and turn . Windows the portable bundle The bundle contains the server, the web client, a Node.js runtime and an empty data/ skeleton. Copy it to any machine with the same operating system, even one without internet access. 1. Unzip it anywhere. 2. Run start server.bat . 3. Edit data/config.json if the host or ports need to change, then restart. Linux and macOS from source ./start server.sh does the same and prefers a bundled runtime when there is one. Use npm run dev while developing; it restarts the server when files change. What the first start creates Path What it is data/dismesh.db The SQLite database users, servers, messages data/config.json The configuration, written with defaults on every start data/certs/ The generated self signed certificate unless you configure your own data/attachments/ , data/avatars/ and similar Uploaded files Ports By default HTTPS listens on 8443 . The plain 8080 port only redirects to HTTPS. Change them with httpsPort and port in data/config.json . See Configuration configuration.html . Running as a service Run the start script under your service manager of choice systemd, a Windows service wrapper, a scheduled task . The process writes its log to standard output. Stop it with a normal termination signal; the database closes cleanly. Backups note One folder Stop the server and copy the whole data/ folder. It contains the database, the configuration, the certificate and every uploaded file. Restore by putting the folder back. Do not copy data/dismesh.db alone while the server runs, because uploads and the database must match. Updating 1. Take a backup. 2. Stop the server. 3. Replace the program files with the new version, keeping your data/ folder. 4. Start the server. Database changes are applied automatically on start. The web client and the phone interface are served by the server, so updating the server updates them everywhere. Desktop and Android apps only need a new release when their own native code changes. Building the portable bundle yourself This produces dist/dismesh portable/ . For Sites, run npm run fetch php once on the build machine to bundle a PHP runtime for Windows. See Sites sites.html . "},{"slug":"configuration","title":"Configuration","desc":"Every key in data/config.json explained, with an example.","group":"Start here","headings":[{"id":"keys","text":"Keys","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"passport-origins","text":"Passport origins","level":2},{"id":"stun-and-turn","text":"STUN and TURN","level":2},{"id":"quick-setup","text":"Quick setup","level":3},{"id":"settings","text":"Settings","level":3},{"id":"external-servers","text":"External servers","level":3}],"text":" data/config.json is created on the first start and rewritten on every start, so any key that is missing gets its default. Restart the server after editing it. Settings that change often session lifetime, upload limits, allowed file types live in the database and are changed from the admin panel. Keys Key Default Meaning port 8080 Plain HTTP port. With HTTPS on it only redirects; with useHttps false it serves the app. httpsPort 8443 Main HTTPS port. publicHost \"localhost\" The name or IP the self signed certificate is issued for. Set it to the address people type, before the first start. useHttps true Set false for plain HTTP on a trusted LAN or for development. Voice, video and notifications need HTTPS in most browsers except on localhost . serverCrt \"\" Path to your own PEM certificate. Empty means use the self signed one. serverKey \"\" Path to the matching private key. Both must be set together. maxUploadMb 25 Upper limit on attachment size. The admin panel can lower it at runtime but never raise it above this value. federation {\"enabled\" false} Federation between servers. Off by default. See Federation federation.html . downloads {\"server\" \"https // \", \"clientDesktop\" \"https // \", \"clientAndroid\" \"https // \", \"website\" \"https // \"} Links shown in the web interface download window and on invite pages. The login screen shows website . server is only recorded. Only https // addresses are used. Replace the https // placeholders and restart the server. passportOrigins Extra origins a Passport proof may be signed for. See below. trustProxy false Express trust proxy value. Set it behind a reverse proxy. pushAllowPrivateEndpoints false Let the server send UnifiedPush wake ups to private network addresses, such as a ntfy on your LAN. iceServers External STUN and TURN servers for WebRTC calls across networks. turn see below The built in STUN/TURN server, off by default. See STUN and TURN stun and turn . sites {\"phpPath\" \"\", \"maxWorkers\" 4} PHP runtime and worker count for Sites sites.html . Example In JSON a backslash must be written as \\\\ , or simply use forward slashes, which work on every operating system. Passport origins A Passport proof is signed for the server's origin, and the server only accepts an origin it recognizes. Accepted origins are loopback hosts localhost , 127.0.0.1 , 1 on any port; http //<publicHost and https //<publicHost built from publicHost , port and httpsPort ; every entry of passportOrigins . So a LAN or domain setup must set publicHost to the address users type, or list the exact origin scheme, host and port, no path in passportOrigins . STUN and TURN Chat and call signaling always go through your MeshCrowd server. Only the audio and video between people needs STUN or TURN, and only when two of them cannot reach each other directly. On one network calls just work. Across routers and NAT a STUN server tells each browser its public address, and behind strict NAT a TURN relay carries the media. MeshCrowd has both built in, with nothing to install. It is off by default , so a LAN only server never opens an extra port. Quick setup 1. Run setup turn.bat Windows, it asks for administrator rights once or ./setup turn.sh Linux and macOS; use sudo so it can open ufw or firewalld . 2. Answer the questions. It can detect your public IP with a single request to a public STUN server, and only if you agree. It saves the settings, opens the firewall on this machine, shows the router forwarding table and proves a relay can be allocated. 3. On your router forward UDP and TCP 3478 and UDP 49152 49999 to this machine. 4. Restart MeshCrowd. To check from outside, join a call from a phone on mobile data. The same settings live in Admin Panel, Calls site administrators enable or disable the server, the external IP with a Detect button, ports, a live status, and a Test button. Changes apply without a restart. setup turn status , disable and remove firewall are also available. Settings The turn section of data/config.json Key Default Meaning enabled false Run the built in server. port 3478 UDP and TCP port clients connect to. tcp true Also accept TCP, which helps behind strict firewalls. The relay itself is UDP. externalIp \"\" The machine's public IPv4 address. Set it when the server is behind a router. advertisedHost \"\" Host name given to clients. Empty uses externalIp , then publicHost . relayPortMin , relayPortMax 49152 , 49999 UDP ports used for relayed streams. credentialTtlSeconds 86400 Lifetime of the per user credentials. allowPrivatePeers false Allow relaying to private addresses. Off so the relay cannot reach into your LAN. maxAllocations , maxAllocationsPerUser 500 , 20 Limits. maxKbps 0 Bandwidth cap per relay, 0 for none. Signed in users receive short lived credentials that expire by themselves, so nothing is stored and a leaked one soon stops working. IPv6 relaying is not supported. External servers You can also use servers you run or rent elsewhere, in Admin Panel, Calls or in iceServers Entries with a user name and password are only given to signed in users. warn Reverse proxies Behind a proxy that terminates TLS set trustProxy to the hop count or subnet , not true . true on a directly exposed server lets clients spoof X Forwarded For . See TLS and reverse proxies tls.html . "},{"slug":"tls","title":"TLS and reverse proxies","desc":"The self-signed certificate, bringing your own, checking fingerprints and running behind nginx or Caddy.","group":"Start here","headings":[{"id":"option-1-the-self-signed-certificate","text":"Option 1: the self-signed certificate","level":2},{"id":"option-2-your-own-certificate","text":"Option 2: your own certificate","level":2},{"id":"checking-the-fingerprint","text":"Checking the fingerprint","level":2},{"id":"behind-a-reverse-proxy","text":"Behind a reverse proxy","level":2},{"id":"calls-across-networks","text":"Calls across networks","level":2}],"text":" MeshCrowd serves HTTPS by default. Browsers only allow microphones, cameras and notifications on secure origins, so TLS matters for voice and video. Option 1 the self signed certificate Leave serverCrt and serverKey empty. On the first start the server creates a ten year certificate for publicHost , localhost and 127.0.0.1 under data/certs/ and reuses it afterwards. Browsers warn once because no authority vouches for it. To move to a new host or IP, change publicHost , delete data/certs/ and restart. Clients that trusted the old certificate show a \"certificate changed\" warning once. Option 2 your own certificate Set both values to PEM files, for example from Let's Encrypt or your company CA Paths are absolute, or relative to the project root. A full chain file is recommended so clients can build the whole chain. The key must match the certificate and be at least 2048 bit RSA or an equivalent EC key. Restart after renewing the files are read once at start. If anything is wrong missing file, invalid PEM, mismatch, weak key the server logs a clear certs error and exits instead of starting without TLS. Checking the fingerprint Every start prints the certificate's SHA 256 fingerprint It matches openssl x509 noout fingerprint sha256 in cert.pem and the fingerprint the desktop and Android clients show when you connect to a self signed server. Compare it out of band before you trust a server you do not recognize. Behind a reverse proxy If nginx, Caddy or another proxy terminates TLS in front of MeshCrowd 1. Run MeshCrowd with \"useHttps\" false on a local port, or keep HTTPS between the proxy and the server. 2. Set \"trustProxy\" to the number of proxies in front for example 1 or to their subnet. 3. Forward Host and X Forwarded Proto , and allow WebSocket upgrades on /ws . 4. Set publicHost to the public name, or add the exact public origin to passportOrigins . warn Why the hop count matters Without trustProxy the server sees every visitor as the proxy, and session cookies are issued without the Secure flag. With trustProxy true on a directly exposed server, clients can fake their address and defeat rate limits and audit logs. Use a hop count or subnet. Calls across networks Voice and video use WebRTC directly between people. Turn on the built in STUN/TURN server or add your own to iceServers see STUN and TURN configuration.html stun and turn . The proxy does not carry media. "},{"slug":"accounts","title":"Accounts, Passport and sign-in","desc":"Registering, the Passport identity file, strengthened sign-in, two-factor authentication and recovery.","group":"Using MeshCrowd","headings":[{"id":"registering-and-signing-in","text":"Registering and signing in","level":2},{"id":"passport-your-portable-identity","text":"Passport: your portable identity","level":2},{"id":"strengthened-sign-in","text":"Strengthened sign-in","level":2},{"id":"two-factor-authentication","text":"Two-factor authentication","level":2},{"id":"changing-your-password","text":"Changing your password","level":2},{"id":"profile","text":"Profile","level":2},{"id":"friends-and-direct-messages","text":"Friends and direct messages","level":2}],"text":" Registering and signing in Anyone who can reach the server can register with an email address, a username and a password. The first account becomes the Owner. You can sign in with your email address or your username. Sessions are opaque tokens kept on the server in an httpOnly cookie. They are not JWTs, so each one can be revoked, and disabling an account ends its sessions and live connections at once. Passport your portable identity When you register in the web client the browser creates a Passport a key pair that anchors your account. Export it from Settings, Passport as an encrypted .mcpass file. Sign in with the file and its passphrase, which is also how you recover a forgotten password. Register on another MeshCrowd server with the same identity. There is one account per Passport per server. warn Keep the file safe Your Passport also protects your encrypted DMs and your private Notes channels. If you lose both the Passport file and your password, that encrypted content cannot be recovered by anyone. Strengthened sign in Accounts created in the web client derive two keys from your password in the browser . One key is sent to the server and stored as a bcrypt hash. The other wraps your Passport seed and never leaves the browser. The server never sees the password of such an account, so logs, a database copy or a curious operator cannot read it. Older accounts, including those created by very old Android apps, can opt in under Settings, Passport . Android apps older than 3.0 cannot sign in to a strengthened account and need to be updated. Failed Passport proofs lock that identity for 15 minutes after five failures. Password login is not affected. Two factor authentication Turn on TOTP under Settings, Account . Scan the QR code with an authenticator app and store the recovery codes somewhere safe each works once. Email verification is not implemented; two factor is TOTP based. Changing your password Use Settings, Account, Change password . For strengthened accounts the browser re wraps your Passport with the new password. Profile Your avatar, banner, bio, custom status and presence are covered in Profiles, status and themes personalization.html . Privacy controls decide who can send you DMs and who can see your profile card. Friends and direct messages Send a friend request by username. Friends can start 1 1 DMs; group DMs hold up to ten people. A 1 1 DM can be switched to end to end encryption with the lock button, which cannot be undone delete the conversation and start a new one to go back. Details are on Security and privacy security.html . "},{"slug":"servers-channels","title":"Servers, channels and roles","desc":"Channel types, categories, the permission system, channel overrides, role icons and Notes channels.","group":"Using MeshCrowd","headings":[{"id":"servers","text":"Servers","level":2},{"id":"invite-links","text":"Invite links","level":3},{"id":"channel-types","text":"Channel types","level":2},{"id":"roles-and-permissions","text":"Roles and permissions","level":2},{"id":"role-colors-and-icons","text":"Role colors and icons","level":3},{"id":"channel-overrides","text":"Channel overrides","level":3},{"id":"notes-channels","text":"Notes channels","level":2},{"id":"server-rail-and-folders","text":"Server rail and folders","level":2},{"id":"welcome-screen-and-events","text":"Welcome screen and events","level":2},{"id":"next","text":"Next","level":2}],"text":" Servers A server is a community members, channels, roles and settings. People join by invite code, by a direct invite from someone's profile card, or from the public server directory. A server can be private invite only or public listed in discovery, optionally auto join . Open Server Settings from the server name at the top of the channel list. Server Settings, Overview ../assets/img/settings overview.jpg Invite links Every invite code also works as a link https //your server 8443/i/<code . It opens a small page with the server's name and icon and its member count when the server is public , a Join in browser button, an Open in app button and the download links the server owner has set. Opening the page never uses up an invite, and joining always asks for confirmation first. Copy link sits next to Copy in the invite window and in Server Settings, Invites for every invite and for the vanity link . Join in browser signs you in or lets you register first, then asks \"Join this server?\". Open in app uses an mcr //your server 8443/<code address. The Windows desktop app and the Android app open it, ask before switching to a different server and ask again before joining. See Desktop app clients.html desktop app windows and Android app android.html . The old way still works paste the code into Add Server, Join with invite . Channel invites and code@domain invites from federated servers work as links too. Channel types Type What it is Public text Anyone with the right to view the server can read and write Private text Visible only to members a role or override lets in Announcement A channel people can read but only managers can post in Read only Like announcement, for rules and information Voice A voice room with camera and screen sharing Stage A voice room split into speakers and audience Forum A channel made of threaded posts Notes A private encrypted notebook for each member Create channels with the + next to Channels and organize them into categories by dragging. A channel can have an icon, a topic and slowmode . A text channel can also be marked age restricted ; see Moderation and safety moderation.html . note Voice quality is fixed at creation Voice and stage channels get a quality preset when they are created Mobile, Low, Medium, High or HD Music . To change it, delete the channel and create a new one. Roles and permissions Roles are sets of permission flags. Everyone has the built in @everyone role, and you can create as many more as you like. A member's permissions are the union of their roles. The Roles tab ../assets/img/settings roles.jpg Permission Allows View Channel, Send Messages, Attach Files Basic reading, writing and uploading Manage Messages Delete and pin other people's messages Manage Channels Create, edit and delete channels, categories and channel webhooks Manage Roles Create roles and assign them Manage Server Rename the server, invites, onboarding, AutoMod, templates, insights Kick Members, Ban Members Remove people Moderate Members Time people out, set slowmode, mute in voice Create Invite, Change Nickname, Manage Nicknames Invites and display names View Audit Log Read the log of moderator actions Prune Content Delete old history in this server Manage Bots Create and edit this server's bots Administrator Everything Nobody can grant a permission they do not hold themselves. The owner always has every permission, and the server enforces this rule rather than the interface. Role colors and icons Each role has a color, and a role icon an emoji or an uploaded image. The icon of a member's highest role that has one is shown next to their name in chat and in the member list. A per member name color override beats the role color. Channel overrides Open a channel's settings to allow or deny permissions for a role or a single member in just that channel. A deny on a channel beats a grant from a role. Notes channels A Notes channel gives every member a private notebook inside the server, with text and up to five attachments per note. Everything is encrypted in the browser with a key derived from your Passport, so the database and the admins cannot read it. Admins can only delete notes older than a date. Notes cannot be searched, forwarded or converted to another channel type, and losing your Passport means losing your notes. Server rail and folders Your server rail is personal drag servers into folders with their own icon and color. Mute a server or a channel, or limit notifications to mentions, from the right click menu. Welcome screen and events The welcome screen lists highlighted channels for new members. Scheduled events have a name, description, location, start and end, and RSVP tracking. Next Put the rules in front of newcomers with Community tools community tools.html . Keep order with Moderation and safety moderation.html . "},{"slug":"messaging","title":"Messaging and search","desc":"Writing, editing, replies, threads, forums, polls, voice and scheduled messages, attachments and search.","group":"Using MeshCrowd","headings":[{"id":"the-basics","text":"The basics","level":2},{"id":"formatting","text":"Formatting","level":3},{"id":"mentions","text":"Mentions","level":3},{"id":"replies-threads-and-forums","text":"Replies, threads and forums","level":2},{"id":"reactions-polls-and-pins","text":"Reactions, polls and pins","level":2},{"id":"attachments","text":"Attachments","level":2},{"id":"voice-messages","text":"Voice messages","level":2},{"id":"scheduled-messages","text":"Scheduled messages","level":2},{"id":"slash-commands","text":"Slash commands","level":2},{"id":"search","text":"Search","level":2},{"id":"notifications","text":"Notifications","level":2},{"id":"incoming-webhooks","text":"Incoming webhooks","level":2}],"text":" A channel with an image, a code block and a poll ../assets/img/chat general.jpg The basics Type in the box at the bottom and press Enter . Use Shift+Enter for a new line. Hover a message for its actions reply, react, thread, edit, pin, forward and more. Press Up in an empty box to edit your last message. Formatting bold , italic , code and fenced code blocks with a language for highlighting. spoiler hides text until clicked. Type and a name for emoji shortcodes, @ for mentions and for channels. Links get a preview card unless you are in an encrypted DM. Mentions @username notifies a person, @rolename a role single word names , and @everyone or @here everyone or the people online. Bots can never ping the whole server. Replies, threads and forums Reply to quote a message. Forward copies a message to another conversation. Threads start from any message and have their own history. The Threads panel lists every thread in a channel. A thread's creator or a channel manager can give it an icon or delete it. Forum channels consist entirely of posts, each with its own thread. Posts show as cards with the author, a preview of the opening message, an image thumbnail, the reaction count and the reply count. A search box finds or starts a post, you can sort by Recent activity or Newest posts , and closed posts carry a Closed badge and accept messages from moderators only. On a wide screen the chosen post opens beside the list; on a phone it opens full screen. A forum channel ../assets/img/forum.jpg Reactions, polls and pins Click a reaction to add yours. Polls take a question and options and show live percentages; you can choose several options when the poll allows it. Pinned messages are listed in the pin panel. Attachments Up to five attachments per message. Still images can be resized before upload Original, 1920, 1280 or 800 pixels , animated GIFs get a play and pause button, and non ASCII file names are kept. The size limit comes from maxUploadMb and the admin panel; some file types executables, HTML, SVG are always refused. Voice messages The microphone button in the composer records up to five minutes. A red bar shows the time; the bin discards the clip and the send button posts it with a small player play, progress, seek . It is recorded as Opus in the browser, desktop app or Android app and needs microphone permission and HTTPS or localhost . Voice messages are not available in end to end encrypted DMs. Scheduled messages The clock button next to the composer opens Send later for what you typed. Pick a time or a preset such as tomorrow at 9 00. The message is posted as you at that moment with the same checks as a normal message, so it can still be refused, for example if you are timed out or AutoMod objects. Failures stay in your list with the reason, and you can cancel anything you scheduled. On the phone interface hold the send button. Encrypted DMs, Notes channels and DMs with people on other servers cannot be scheduled. Slash commands Type / to see the commands you can use. Built in commands include /me , /nick , /shrug , /spoiler , /thread , /topic and /help . Bots can add their own; see Slash commands slash commands.html . Search Open search from the magnifier. Tick which fields to match message text full text search , usernames , channel names and attachment file names . Results open at the message in its channel. Search covers only conversations you can see; Notes channels and encrypted DMs are not searchable, and age restricted channels are left out until you confirm your age. Search results ../assets/img/search.jpg Notifications Each channel and DM can be muted, set to mentions only, or to everything the default is mentions for channels and everything for DMs . Desktop notifications use the browser or the desktop app. The tray icon of the desktop app shows an unread badge. On Android see the Android app android.html . A chat you open with unread messages shows a red New line above the first one; see Profiles, status and themes personalization.html unread messages for its settings. Incoming webhooks A channel manager can create incoming webhooks under the channel's settings. A script POST s JSON to the webhook URL and a message appears with the webhook's name and avatar. See Bots, API and webhooks bots api.html . "},{"slug":"voice-video","title":"Voice, video and stages","desc":"How calls work, quality presets, camera and screen sharing, stage channels, noise suppression and troubleshooting.","group":"Using MeshCrowd","headings":[{"id":"how-calls-work","text":"How calls work","level":2},{"id":"joining","text":"Joining","level":2},{"id":"quality-presets","text":"Quality presets","level":2},{"id":"camera-and-screen-sharing","text":"Camera and screen sharing","level":2},{"id":"stage-channels","text":"Stage channels","level":2},{"id":"moderator-tools","text":"Moderator tools","level":2},{"id":"private-calls","text":"Private calls","level":2},{"id":"soundboard","text":"Soundboard","level":2},{"id":"noise-suppression","text":"Noise suppression","level":2},{"id":"troubleshooting-calls","text":"Troubleshooting calls","level":2}],"text":" A voice channel with camera tiles ../assets/img/voice call.jpg How calls work Voice and video are peer to peer WebRTC . Every participant connects directly to every other participant, and the server only relays the signaling over the same WebSocket used for chat. There is no media server to host. note Plan for the size of the call Because it is a full mesh, each person uploads their stream once per other participant. A call of roughly eight or more people with video asks a lot of everybody's upload bandwidth. Audio only rooms scale much further. Joining Click a voice channel and press Join voice . Allow microphone access when the browser asks. Use the controls to mute, deafen, turn the camera on, share your screen, open the soundboard or leave. Calls need HTTPS or localhost , and people on different networks need a STUN or TURN server see Configuration configuration.html . On each participant's tile you get a speaking ring and a live level strip. Each person's tile has its own volume slider. The participant grid uses large tiles and scrolls when a room is full. In a voice channel the call panel sits above the text chat; drag the divider between them up or down to give the room or the chat more space. Your height is remembered in the browser. Stage channels use the same large, scrollable tiles. On a phone the call is a full screen of two column tiles, with the text chat one tap away. Quality presets The creator picks a preset when the channel is created. It is fixed afterwards to change it, delete the channel and create a new one. Preset Sample rate Bitrate Use Mobile 8 kHz 12 kbps Poor connections and phones on mobile data Low 16 kHz 24 kbps Speech on a weak line Medium 24 kHz 48 kbps The default High 48 kHz 96 kbps Clear speech HD / Music 48 kHz stereo 192 kbps Music and shared audio Camera and screen sharing Camera and screen share are separate tiles, so you can show both at once. Any video tile has a fullscreen button. The desktop app uses the system's screen and window picker; in a browser the browser's own picker appears. On a phone the camera has a flip button and screen sharing is not offered. Stage channels A stage is a voice room split into speakers and an audience . The audience is muted until a speaker or moderator invites them. Audience members can raise a hand ; a moderator can invite them to speak or move them back to the audience. Stages work well for town halls and announcements. Moderator tools Members with Moderate Members can mute for everyone from another person's tile. The target's client stops sending audio and their own unmute button is disabled until a moderator lifts it; a badge shows on the tile. Without a media server this works by instructing the target's client, as in other chat apps. Private calls Direct messages and group DMs support calls too. A DM call never appears on the \"in a call\" indicator of the member list or anywhere outside the DM's own members. Soundboard A server can have a soundboard of short clips that members with permission can play into the call. Manage it under Server Settings, Soundboard . Noise suppression Settings, Voice, Advanced noise suppression RNNoise runs your microphone through a small neural network compiled to WebAssembly, which removes keyboard, fan and background noise. It works on your own device, adds about ten milliseconds of delay and is off by default. The module about 5 MB is only downloaded the first time a call starts with it on. If it cannot start, the call simply continues without it. Troubleshooting calls Symptom What to check No microphone prompt The page is not on HTTPS or localhost Connects on the LAN but not across networks Turn on the built in STUN/TURN server setup turn.bat , or Admin Panel, Calls and forward the ports on the router, see STUN and TURN configuration.html stun and turn One person cannot be heard Their browser blocked the microphone, or their input device is wrong in the device picker Choppy audio in a big call Lower the preset, or ask people to turn cameras off "},{"slug":"personalization","title":"Profiles, status and themes","desc":"Your profile card, presence and custom status, notification sounds, themes, layout and language.","group":"Using MeshCrowd","headings":[{"id":"your-profile","text":"Your profile","level":2},{"id":"presence-and-custom-status","text":"Presence and custom status","level":2},{"id":"themes","text":"Themes","level":2},{"id":"layout","text":"Layout","level":2},{"id":"when-you-open-meshcrowd","text":"When you open MeshCrowd","level":2},{"id":"unread-messages","text":"Unread messages","level":2},{"id":"language","text":"Language","level":2},{"id":"names-and-nicknames","text":"Names and nicknames","level":2}],"text":" Your profile Open Settings from the gear in the bottom left. You can set an avatar, a banner image or color, a bio and a display name. A profile card appears when someone clicks your name. A profile card ../assets/img/profile.jpg Privacy settings decide who can send you direct messages and who can see your profile card. You can also choose whether you appear in the discovery directory. Presence and custom status Choose Online , Idle , Do not disturb or Invisible , and add a custom status with an emoji and text. The slash command /afk sets idle with a message. Notification sounds follow your presence by default online and idle chime, do not disturb stays silent , and you can override that per account. Themes Every member picks their own look under Settings, Appearance . Start with a preset and adjust the colors, or build your own Presets MeshCrowd Dark, MeshCrowd Light, Midnight Purple, Forest, Sunset and High Contrast. Colors for the brand, the rail, the sidebar, the chat background and the text. Fonts default, serif, monospace and a few more. An optional background gradient start, end and angle behind the sidebar, chat and member list. Copy CSS exports your theme as a snippet that someone else can import. Midnight Purple theme ../assets/img/theme purple.jpg Themes are validated to be plain colors and a font choice. They never carry arbitrary CSS, so a shared theme cannot load external resources. Layout Drag the edges of the channel list and the member list to resize them; the sizes are saved with your account. The server rail can be arranged with folders. When you open MeshCrowd Under Settings, Appearance choose what the app shows at start the Home screen, or Resume where I left off the last server and channel you used . Unread messages When you open a channel or DM that has messages you have not read, a red line with the date and a New badge marks the first unread message, and the view jumps there instead of to the bottom. The line stays while the chat is open and is gone the next time you open it. Four settings under Settings, Appearance tune it The \"new messages\" line show or hide it. When opening a chat with unread messages jump to the first unread message, or stay at the latest one. Messages shown above the line 0 to 50 how much context stays visible above the first unread message when you jump. Messages loaded when opening a chat 20 to 100 how many of the latest messages are fetched. If more messages than that are unread, the line sits at the top of the loaded page and you scroll up for the rest. The settings are saved with your account, so they apply in the browser, the desktop app and the phone interface alike. Language The interface speaks English and Hungarian. Change it in your settings, or from the selector on the sign in page. Administrators can add more languages from the admin panel. Names and nicknames A server can give you a nickname that only shows there. Server admins can set a per member name color that beats the role color. "},{"slug":"clients","title":"Web, desktop and phone clients","desc":"What each client offers, how the desktop app pins certificates, and how the phone interface is served.","group":"Using MeshCrowd","headings":[{"id":"web","text":"Web","level":2},{"id":"desktop-app-windows","text":"Desktop app (Windows)","level":2},{"id":"phone-interface","text":"Phone interface","level":2},{"id":"language-and-themes","text":"Language and themes","level":2}],"text":" All clients talk to the same server and show the same data. Pick whichever suits the moment. Client Best for Notes Web Everything, nothing to install Every feature, in any modern browser Desktop Windows Daily use at a desk Tray badge, native notifications, certificate pinning Android On the go Phone interface, local notifications, optional UnifiedPush Web Open the server address. Sign in and you have every feature. Add it to your home screen from the browser menu if you like. Phone browsers are served the phone interface automatically; add ?ui=desktop or ?ui=mobile to the address to switch. Desktop app Windows A portable app unzip it and run MeshCrowd.exe . On the first launch it asks for a server address such as https //192.168.1.10 8443 , then loads the same interface as the browser and adds A tray icon with a live unread badge colored by your presence. Colors are customizable under Settings, Desktop App, Tray Icon . A connecting screen with a spinner while the server answers. If it cannot be reached or takes over 20 seconds it offers Retry and Change server instead of a blank window. Native notifications , close to tray and start with Windows. The operating system's screen and window picker for screen sharing. Invite links mcr // links from an invite page open in the app. The app registers itself for them on every start, which also repairs the entry after you move the folder; switch it off under Settings, Desktop App . Links always ask before switching server and before joining. register mcr protocol.bat and unregister mcr protocol.bat next to MeshCrowd.exe do the same by hand. Trust on first use certificate pinning for self signed servers the first time you confirm the fingerprint, and a later change raises a warning. A certificate from a public authority is accepted normally. The app stores its settings in a data folder next to the executable, so the whole folder can live on a USB stick. It carries no server and no web files of its own updating the server updates the interface. To run it from source for development npm install then npm run electron . Phone interface The server serves a phone first interface at /m/ , used by Android browsers and by the Android app. It has four tabs Servers, Messages, Notifications, You , long press menus, bottom sheets, voice messages, polls, scheduling by holding the send button, slash command chips and calls. See the Android app android.html guide for installation and notifications. The phone interface ../assets/img/m chat.jpg Language and themes Language and theme are saved per account, so they follow you from client to client. "},{"slug":"android","title":"Android app","desc":"Installing the APK, connecting to a self-signed server, notification modes including UnifiedPush, and building it yourself.","group":"Using MeshCrowd","headings":[{"id":"installing","text":"Installing","level":2},{"id":"using-it","text":"Using it","level":2},{"id":"what-works-on-the-phone","text":"What works on the phone","level":2},{"id":"notifications-without-google-services","text":"Notifications without Google services","level":2},{"id":"unifiedpush","text":"UnifiedPush","level":3},{"id":"building-the-apk-yourself","text":"Building the APK yourself","level":2},{"id":"known-limits","text":"Known limits","level":2}],"text":" The Android app is a thin Kotlin shell Android 8.0 or newer, one universal APK, no native libraries around the phone interface your server serves at /m/ . Because the whole interface comes from your server, updating the server updates every phone and a new APK is only needed when the shell itself changes. Installing 1. Download the APK on your phone and open it. Android asks you once to allow installs from your browser or file manager. 2. Open the app and type your server address chat.example.com , 192.168.1.44 8080 , or with http // or https // . HTTPS is tried first. 3. A self signed certificate is trusted once, by its SHA 256 fingerprint. Compare it with the fingerprint your server prints at start before you accept. 4. A plain http address is allowed, with a warning. Calls and notifications need HTTPS. Using it Keyboard and files tapping a field raises the keyboard; attachments use the system file picker; downloads including decrypted DM files go to the Downloads folder with a notification. Invite links tapping an mcr // link the Open in app button on an invite page opens the app. For the server the app is already set up for it asks to join; for another server it asks first, shows the connect screen with the address filled in, and asks to join once connected. Needs version 3.9 or newer. Back button closes sheets and screens first. On another tab it goes back to the Servers tab, and from Servers it exits. Calls voice, camera and DM calls work in the phone interface. The app asks for microphone and camera permission for your server only. Changing server the You tab has an option to disconnect and enter another address. Start view under You , Open on start , choose the tab the app opens on Servers, Messages, Notifications or You or the last chat you had open. Message style choose plain chat or chat bubbles under You . Administration asks for your password opening the Admin Panel or Server Settings asks you to confirm your password first, so a phone left unlocked does not hand over the administration screens. What works on the phone The phone interface covers the same features as the desktop one Messaging channels, threads custom channel and thread icons show in the lists and the chat header , forum channels cards with search, sorting and previews that open as threads , direct and group chats with encryption, reactions, replies, polls, voice messages, stickers, slash commands, scheduled messages and saved messages. The emoji button opens the full picker with categories, search, recents, custom emoji and shortcode suggestions, and the sticker picker has search. A red New line marks the first unread message when you open a chat; see Unread messages personalization.html unread messages . Notes channels your encrypted journal and Sites open full screen. Voice voice rooms and stages, camera, soundboard and a live list of who is in each room right under the channel. Server management the server menu has Events, Server Settings roles, channels, members, invites, AutoMod, bots, onboarding, audit log and the rest , Create Channel and Create Category, shown only to people with the permission. Your account the You tab opens account, appearance themes , voice and video, privacy, Passport and security settings, saved and scheduled messages, and the Admin Panel for site administrators, including federation. Federated servers from paired instances appear in the server list with a globe badge; long press one to leave it. Settings and admin screens use the same pages as the desktop app, laid out as a scrolling tab strip with the content below. Notifications without Google services The app polls your server itself, so it needs no Firebase or Google Play Services. There are three modes, all selectable under You, Android app Mode How it works Battery Periodic check WorkManager every 15 minutes or longer Very light Fast mode on by default A foreground service with a permanent notification, polling every 1 to 1440 minutes Heavier UnifiedPush The server wakes the phone through a distributor app such as ntfy Light and instant The permanent notification of fast mode comes back by itself if you swipe it away Android 14 and newer allow dismissing it . While the app is open, messages arrive instantly over the WebSocket. Encrypted DMs show only a generic \"New encrypted message\". Tapping a notification opens that conversation. UnifiedPush 1. Install a UnifiedPush distributor, for example ntfy self hosted or public . 2. In the app open You, Android app, Push notifications and turn it on, choosing your distributor. 3. The server then sends a fixed wake up {\"t\" \"wake\"} to the address the distributor gave the app. The message text never passes through the distributor the app wakes up and fetches notifications itself. note A ntfy on your own network Addresses on private networks are refused by default because users supply them. If your ntfy runs on your LAN, set pushAllowPrivateEndpoints to true in data/config.json . The periodic check keeps running as a safety net, so set it to a long interval when you use UnifiedPush. Building the APK yourself You need JDK 17 and the Android SDK platform 35 and build tools 35 . Set sdk.dir in android/local.properties , then collectApk builds the release APK and copies it to AndroidReleases/MeshCrowd <version .apk . Release builds are signed with a key you create meshcrowd.jks , configured in keystore.properties ; both stay out of version control . Keep a backup of that key an update must be signed with the same one. ./gradlew testDebugUnitTest runs the unit tests. Known limits Older apps before 3.0 cannot sign in to an account that uses strengthened sign in. Update the app. Screen sharing is not available on phones. "},{"slug":"moderation","title":"Moderation and safety","desc":"AutoMod, rules screening, verification levels, age-restricted channels, timeouts, bans, reports, the audit log and data pruning.","group":"Running a community","headings":[{"id":"automod","text":"AutoMod","level":2},{"id":"rules-screening-onboarding","text":"Rules screening (onboarding)","level":2},{"id":"verification-level","text":"Verification level","level":2},{"id":"age-restricted-channels","text":"Age-restricted channels","level":2},{"id":"members-timeouts-kicks-and-bans","text":"Members: timeouts, kicks and bans","level":2},{"id":"reports","text":"Reports","level":2},{"id":"audit-log","text":"Audit log","level":2},{"id":"data-pruning","text":"Data pruning","level":2},{"id":"good-practice","text":"Good practice","level":2}],"text":" MeshCrowd gives moderators tools that act before a problem spreads and keep a record afterwards. Most are under Server Settings . AutoMod Server Settings, AutoMod needs Manage Server . Rules are checked before a message is posted in a channel or thread, and again when a message is edited. AutoMod rules ../assets/img/settings automod.jpg Rule What it catches Blocked words Words or phrases, whole word or substring, with wildcards Links Block all links, allow only listed sites, or block listed sites subdomains included Mass mentions Too many people or roles in one message; @everyone and @here always count as too many Spam Too many messages in a window, or the same message repeated Capitals Too large a share of capital letters A hit refuses the message, names the rule to the author, logs it author, channel and the first 200 characters and, if the rule says so, times the author out . Each rule can exempt roles and channels. The owner and anyone who can manage messages in the channel are never filtered. Bots and webhooks are not filtered. The log keeps the latest 500 hits per server. note No regular expressions Rules deliberately do not accept user written regular expressions, which could be crafted to hang the server. Use wildcards instead. Rules screening onboarding Turn on Require new members to accept the rules under Server Settings, Onboarding . New members see a welcome window with the rules, up to five questions whose answers hand out roles, and an \"I agree\" box. Until they accept they can read what their roles show but cannot post, react, attach files or join voice, and choosing Later keeps them in that view only state. Members who are already in are not affected. Roles with moderation or management powers can never be handed out by a question. What a new member sees ../assets/img/onboarding.jpg Verification level Server Settings, Overview, Verification level holds back brand new accounts and recent joiners from posting Level Requires None Nothing Low An account at least 5 minutes old Medium Account 5 minutes old and a member for 10 minutes High Account 7 days old and a member for 10 minutes The owner, bots and anyone who holds a role other than @everyone are never held back. Everything is local there is no email or phone check. Age restricted channels Tick Age restricted channel 18+ when creating or editing a text channel. The channel gets an 18+ badge, and the first time a member opens one they confirm I am 18 or older once for their whole account. It is a plain click through nothing is verified and nothing is sent to anyone. Unconfirmed members cannot read or post there, and the channel is left out of their search. An age restricted channel ../assets/img/age gate.jpg warn A courtesy gate, not access control The gate does not stop an unconfirmed member's client from receiving live events for the channel. To keep people out of a channel, use channel permissions and private channels. Members timeouts, kicks and bans From a member's right click menu or Server Settings, Members Timeout stops someone posting or speaking for a while needs Moderate Members . Kick removes someone, who can rejoin with an invite. Ban removes someone and blocks them from rejoining. Slowmode limits how often people can post in a channel. Mute for everyone in voice rooms. Reports Any member can report a message or a person. Reports go to a queue that site administrators with the reports permission can resolve from the admin panel. Audit log Server Settings, Audit Log lists what moderators did role and channel changes, kicks, bans, invites, AutoMod rule edits and more, with who and when. Data pruning Delete message history older than a chosen date. Server moderators with Prune Content can do it for their own server; site administrators can do it instance wide. Every prune shows a preview message count, attachments and size first and can run now or after a 24 hour notice that gives members time to save things. A notice is always posted in the affected conversation, and attachments can be kept or deleted too. Good practice Start with a clear rules message and onboarding. Turn on a verification level on public servers. Give moderators a role with only the permissions they need. Review the AutoMod log now and then to tune rules. "},{"slug":"community-tools","title":"Community tools","desc":"Invites and vanity links, templates, reaction roles, scheduled events and insights.","group":"Running a community","headings":[{"id":"invites-and-vanity-links","text":"Invites and vanity links","level":2},{"id":"server-templates","text":"Server templates","level":2},{"id":"reaction-roles","text":"Reaction roles","level":2},{"id":"onboarding","text":"Onboarding","level":2},{"id":"scheduled-events","text":"Scheduled events","level":2},{"id":"insights","text":"Insights","level":2},{"id":"welcome-screen","text":"Welcome screen","level":2},{"id":"custom-emoji-stickers-and-soundboard","text":"Custom emoji, stickers and soundboard","level":2}],"text":" Invites and vanity links Server Settings, Invites creates extra invite links, each with its own expiry and use limit. The permanent invite code in Overview keeps working. Invites and the vanity link ../assets/img/settings invites.jpg Expiry from one minute to 90 days, or never. Maximum uses 1 to 1000, or unlimited. A use only counts when someone actually joins. Limits at most 25 active invites per member and 100 per server. Vanity link a short name 3 to 32 letters, digits and hyphens people can type instead of a code. It never expires; clear it to stop it working. Direct invites can be sent from a person's profile card, and channel invites give access to just one channel. An expired or used up invite tells the person so instead of failing silently. Server templates Server Settings, Templates saves the structure of the server as a template with a share code roles with their permissions, categories, channels, channel permissions and the rules text. Anyone who pastes the code in the Template code field when creating a server gets a brand new private server with that structure and becomes its owner. Members, messages, emoji, bots and invites are never copied. After you change your server, Update refreshes the template. Reaction roles Server Settings, Reaction roles needs Manage Roles . Choose a channel and one of its recent messages, an emoji and a role. Members who react with that emoji get the role and lose it when they remove the reaction. The emoji is placed on the message for you. Tick Exclusive so that the emojis of one message behave like a single choice. Roles with moderation or management powers cannot be used. Members who still have to accept the server rules cannot react. Reaction roles ../assets/img/settings reactionroles.jpg Onboarding See Moderation and safety moderation.html rules screening onboarding rules, questions that hand out roles and acceptance before posting. Scheduled events Create a server event with a name, description, location, optional linked channel and start and end times. Members can mark themselves interested , and changes are broadcast live. Insights Server Settings, Insights needs Manage Server shows member count and growth, messages per day and per hour of day, the busiest channels, the most active members and how many people were active this week, for the last 7, 14, 30 or 90 days. Insights ../assets/img/settings insights.jpg Everything is computed from the messages and memberships that already exist. Nothing extra is tracked. Times are UTC and the numbers refresh about once a minute. Welcome screen Highlight a few channels with a short description each, so a new member knows where to start. Open Server Settings, Welcome Screen . Custom emoji, stickers and soundboard Upload your own emoji and stickers images and a soundboard of short clips under Server Settings . Emoji work in messages and reactions; stickers are sent as a message; the soundboard plays into voice rooms. Animated stickers GIF, APNG, animated WebP stay still in the picker and the sticker editors until you hover them, and in chat only the six newest on screen play at once; hover any sticker to play it. "},{"slug":"bots-api","title":"Bots, API and webhooks","desc":"AI bots, bot tokens, the bot API, signed outgoing webhooks, incoming webhooks and an n8n recipe.","group":"Extending","headings":[{"id":"creating-a-bot","text":"Creating a bot","level":2},{"id":"ai-bots","text":"AI bots","level":2},{"id":"the-bot-token","text":"The bot token","level":2},{"id":"bot-api","text":"Bot API","level":2},{"id":"outgoing-webhooks","text":"Outgoing webhooks","level":2},{"id":"an-n8n-recipe","text":"An n8n recipe","level":2},{"id":"incoming-webhooks","text":"Incoming webhooks","level":2},{"id":"good-practice","text":"Good practice","level":2}],"text":" A bot is a special account that belongs to one server. Its name carries a BOT badge and it cannot sign in. One bot can do two jobs at the same time An AI chat partner backed by Ollama or any OpenAI compatible service. It answers mentions and, if you allow it, private DMs. An integration driven by the Bot API and signed webhooks , for n8n, scripts and your own tools. Bots in Server Settings ../assets/img/settings bots.jpg Creating a bot Server administrators with Manage Bots create bots under Server Settings, Bots . Site administrators can also create them for any server in the admin panel. A bot has a name, an avatar, an optional AI provider and model, a persona the system prompt , mention on or off, DM mode on or off and the number of recent messages it sees. Leave the provider empty for an API only bot. AI bots Providers are set up by a site administrator under Admin, AI a kind Ollama or OpenAI compatible , a base URL, an optional API key stored encrypted and never shown again , an optional model allowlist press Test connection to fetch the list , a timeout and a parallel request limit. Tick Server admins may use this provider to offer it to server admins. warn Privacy Everything a bot is asked is sent to its provider. Bots never read end to end encrypted DMs, group DMs or Notes channels, and only see channels their role can view. Their output cannot mention anyone and has no tools or actions. On a CPU only host use small models about 3 to 4 billion parameters , or point the provider at an Ollama running on a stronger machine. Limits one request per provider at a time by default, at most five waiting, a ten second cooldown per user and bot, and replies capped at 4000 characters. The bot token Open a bot and press Generate token . The token it starts with mcb is shown once ; only its SHA 256 hash is stored. Regenerating it stops the old one working. Send it as a header A bot sees only its own server, only what its roles allow, never Notes channels and never encrypted or group DMs. Limits are 120 requests and 30 writes per minute per bot 429 with Retry After . @everyone and @here in bot messages are defused. Bot API Request Purpose GET /api/bot/me Who the bot is and its webhook state GET /api/bot/channels Channels the bot can view GET /api/bot/messages?scopeType=channel&scopeId=7&limit=50 Read an oldest first page of messages POST /api/bot/messages Post a message PATCH /api/bot/messages/ id Edit one of the bot's own messages DELETE /api/bot/messages/ id Delete one of the bot's own messages PUT /api/bot/commands Publish slash commands see Slash commands slash commands.html POST /api/bot/interactions/ id/respond Answer a slash command Posting a message scopeType is channel , thread or dm a DM needs the bot's DM mode on . Content is up to 4000 characters. The complete reference is in docs/API.md in the repository. Outgoing webhooks Give a bot a webhook URL and MeshCrowd sends it a signed JSON event whenever something it should hear about happens. In the bot's settings choose which messages count mentions an @mention, a reply to the bot, or a DM or all messages in channels it can see. Create the signing secret with Rotate secret ; it is shown once. Every delivery is a POST with these headers Header Meaning X MeshCrowd Event message create , command or ping X MeshCrowd Delivery A unique id for this delivery X MeshCrowd Timestamp Unix seconds X MeshCrowd Signature sha256= followed by the HMAC SHA256 of <timestamp .<raw body keyed with the secret Verify the signature and reject deliveries whose timestamp is more than a few minutes old A message event looks like this Messages written by bots never trigger a delivery, so bots cannot loop. Events for one bot are delivered in order. A 5xx, 429, 408 or network error is retried three attempts in total, after about 0, 5 and 30 seconds ; other 4xx answers are not retried; at most 50 events wait per bot. The URL may carry a path and query but no credentials, redirects are not followed, and a private address localhost or LAN is allowed only if a site administrator saved the URL. Use Send test event to check your receiver. An n8n recipe 1. Add a Webhook trigger node method POST and paste its production URL into the bot. 2. Optionally verify the signature in a Code node. 3. Answer with an HTTP Request node POST https //your host/api/bot/messages , header Authorization Bot <token , JSON body {\"scopeType\" \"channel\", \"scopeId\" {{ $json.body.channel.id }}, \"content\" \"...\", \"replyToMessageId\" {{ $json.body.message.id }}} . For a thread use scopeType \"thread\" with the event's threadId , and for a DM scopeType \"dm\" with its dmId . Incoming webhooks A simpler tool for scripts that only post a channel manager creates an incoming webhook in the channel's settings and gets a URL. POST JSON to it and a message appears under the webhook's name and avatar. No bot or token is needed. Good practice Keep tokens and secrets out of repositories; rotate them if they leak. Give a bot a role with only the channels it needs. Handle 429 by waiting for Retry After . "},{"slug":"slash-commands","title":"Slash commands","desc":"Built-in commands, how bots publish their own, options, private answers and a complete example.","group":"Extending","headings":[{"id":"built-in-commands","text":"Built-in commands","level":2},{"id":"using-a-bot-s-command","text":"Using a bot's command","level":2},{"id":"publishing-commands-for-bot-authors","text":"Publishing commands (for bot authors)","level":2},{"id":"receiving-a-use","text":"Receiving a use","level":3},{"id":"answering","text":"Answering","level":3},{"id":"a-complete-example","text":"A complete example","level":3},{"id":"limits","text":"Limits","level":2}],"text":" Type / in a server channel to see the commands you can use. The list mixes the built in commands with those published by bots . On the phone interface, matching commands appear as chips above the composer. The slash command popup ../assets/img/slash popup.jpg Built in commands Command Does /me <action Posts an action in italics /nick name Changes your nickname on this server /shrug , /tableflip , /unflip Adds the classic text faces /spoiler <text Posts text hidden behind a spoiler /thread <name Starts a thread /topic text Shows or sets the channel topic with permission /dm , /msg <username message Opens or writes a direct message /afk message Sets you to idle with a message /invite Shows an invite /ping , /help Connectivity check and the command list Using a bot's command Pick a command from the popup arrow keys and Tab , or click it . Options are filled in order, and the last text option takes the rest of the line , so no quotes are needed You can also name any option /roll sides 20 note raid boss . If a required option is missing you are told which one and your text is kept. If two bots offer the same command name, the popup shows name@botname . When you press Enter the command goes to the bot, which answers in one of two ways A normal message , posted by the bot and headed \"Mara used /roll\". A private ephemeral answer that only you can see. It is shown in the channel with \"Only you can see this\", is never stored , and disappears when you press Dismiss or reload. A public and a private answer ../assets/img/slash answer.jpg Publishing commands for bot authors A bot needs a token and a working webhook see Bots, API and webhooks bots api.html . Only bots with an enabled webhook show up in the popup, because that is how they hear about a use. The call replaces the whole list . Rules at most 25 commands with 10 options each; names use a z , 0 9 , and up to 32 characters; option type is string default , integer or boolean ; required options must come first. Receiving a use The webhook gets an event of type command Options arrive already converted to their types, and the server has checked that required ones are present. Answering Set \"ephemeral\" true for a private answer. An interaction is valid for 15 minutes and takes at most five answers, so a bot can send an acknowledgement and a follow up. A complete example Limits Commands work in server channels, not in threads or DMs. A member needs permission to send messages in the channel, and must not be timed out or held back by a verification level. Using commands is limited to 10 per 10 seconds per person. "},{"slug":"sites","title":"Sites (PHP intranet)","desc":"Host small PHP, HTML and JS pages inside your server, with a code editor and a visual editor.","group":"Extending","headings":[{"id":"who-can-create-and-edit","text":"Who can create and edit","level":2},{"id":"the-php-runtime","text":"The PHP runtime","level":2},{"id":"the-editor","text":"The editor","level":2},{"id":"external-origins","text":"External origins","level":2},{"id":"links","text":"Links","level":2}],"text":" A Site is a server kind that serves a folder of PHP, HTML, CSS and JS pages inside the app instead of chat channels. It appears in the server rail for everybody a public, auto join server with no channels, voice or notifications and renders in a same origin frame. Use it for a team wiki, a duty rota, a small internal tool. Who can create and edit Site staff with the Manage Any Server or Site Administrator permission create Sites from the + dialog, on the New Site tab. The Site's owner and site staff can edit it; everybody else just views it. The PHP runtime Windows run npm run fetch php once on the build machine. It downloads the portable PHP 8.4 checksum verified and Microsoft's Visual C++ redistributable into runtime/php/ , and npm run build portable copies it along. If PHP exits with the missing DLL code at start, the server runs the bundled vc redist.x64.exe itself Windows shows a UAC prompt unless the server is elevated . Linux and macOS install PHP with your package manager, or set sites.phpPath . Settings in data/config.json Key Default Meaning sites.phpPath \"\" Explicit PHP binary. Empty means runtime/php/php.exe , then php on the PATH sites.maxWorkers 4 Parallel PHP processes per Site 1 to 16 . Each active worker uses roughly 20 to 30 MB The editor The Edit button opens a file tree with a code view CodeMirror with HTML, PHP, JS and CSS coloring, and Ctrl+S and a visual view TinyMCE in which PHP blocks stay protected as chips and are restored byte for byte. A page the visual editor cannot round trip falls back to the code view automatically. Allowed files php html htm css js json txt md svg png jpg jpeg gif webp ico , up to 2 MB per file, 200 files and 50 MB per Site. External origins A Site's settings list the extra https // origins its pages may load scripts, styles, images and frames from. Adding one shows a warning, because a script loaded from another origin runs with the page's privileges. Wildcards are not allowed. Links Links that leave the Site another origin, target=\" blank\" , window.open open in the operating system's browser in the desktop app and in a new tab on the web. danger Trust Site pages run as part of MeshCrowd. Anyone who can edit a Site can run code on the server and, through same origin JavaScript, as the people viewing it. Only give edit rights to people you would give server access. "},{"slug":"federation","title":"Federation","desc":"Pairing two servers so people can reach each other, what is shared, and the safety rules behind it.","group":"Extending","headings":[{"id":"turning-it-on","text":"Turning it on","level":2},{"id":"pairing","text":"Pairing","level":2},{"id":"what-federation-shares","text":"What federation shares","level":2},{"id":"what-it-does-not-do-yet","text":"What it does not do yet","level":2},{"id":"safety-rules","text":"Safety rules","level":2}],"text":" Federation lets two MeshCrowd servers trust each other so that their people can interact. It is off by default a stand alone server opens no federation route and runs no federation worker. Passport sign in works either way. Turning it on Set \"federation\" { \"enabled\" true } in data/config.json and restart. A Federation page appears in the admin panel. Pairing 1. A site administrator sets the federation admin password the first time signed in, or from the server machine . An anonymous visitor cannot claim it. 2. Create an invite link on one server and redeem it on the other. 3. Each side must explicitly accept the other in Admin, Federation . A pending peer can do nothing except finish or cancel its own pairing. 4. Revoke at any time. Revoking drops trust on both sides. What federation shares Friend requests and DMs between people on paired servers. Discovery each other's public servers appear in the directory. Joining you can join a server on another instance with a code@domain invite. Remote servers appear in your server rail and open in a simplified view with text channels, history, posting, editing, deleting and reactions. Remote servers are proxied live from the owning instance nothing is copied. They grey out while that instance is offline. What it does not do yet Remote servers have text channels only no attachments, threads, voice or member list. Federated DMs are not end to end encrypted. Safety rules Peers are trusted only for identity . Permissions are always decided by the instance that owns the server. Calls between instances are signed and rate limited. Outgoing calls refuse redirects and pin the validated address, so a paired peer cannot point your server at your internal network. "},{"slug":"administration","title":"Administration and backups","desc":"The admin panel, staff ranks, upload limits, pruning, languages, backups and day-to-day running.","group":"Operating a server","headings":[{"id":"the-admin-panel","text":"The admin panel","level":2},{"id":"attachments","text":"Attachments","level":2},{"id":"sessions","text":"Sessions","level":2},{"id":"data-pruning","text":"Data pruning","level":2},{"id":"languages","text":"Languages","level":2},{"id":"backups","text":"Backups","level":2},{"id":"updating","text":"Updating","level":2},{"id":"monitoring","text":"Monitoring","level":2},{"id":"moving-to-a-new-machine","text":"Moving to a new machine","level":2}],"text":" The admin panel The admin panel is shown only to accounts with a site staff rank . The Owner the first account has every permission and can create ranks and hand out specific permissions. Permission Allows View Admin Panel See the panel Manage Users Disable and enable accounts, edit any profile Manage Site Roles Create and assign staff ranks Delete Any Message Remove content anywhere Manage Any Server Delete or transfer any server, create Sites Manage Reports Work the user report queue Prune Data Bulk delete history by date Manage AI Configure AI providers and bots on any server Site Administrator Bypasses all site permission checks The panel also shows instance statistics and lets you manage users and servers. Attachments Under Admin, Overview you can lower the upload size limit at runtime never above maxUploadMb in the configuration and optionally restrict uploads to an allowlist of extensions such as .png, .jpg, .pdf . Executables, HTML and SVG are always blocked, and files are served as downloads under a sandboxing Content Security Policy so an upload can never run as script in the app's origin. Sessions Session lifetime is a site setting. Individual sessions are revocable, and disabling an account ends its sessions and live connections immediately. Data pruning Server moderators with Prune Content prune their own server's channels and threads from Server Settings . Site administrators with Prune Data can prune any server's channels or any DM from the admin panel. Conversations are listed by size, and message content is never shown. Group DM creators can prune their own group. Every prune shows a preview first and can run immediately or after a 24 hour notice. See Moderation and safety moderation.html data pruning . Languages The interface ships in English and Hungarian. Administrators can add language files from the admin panel. Strings are plain JSON, so a translation is a copy of the English file with the values changed. Backups note A backup is a folder Stop the server and copy the whole data/ folder the database, the configuration, the certificate and every uploaded file. To restore, put the folder back. Schedule it with the tool of your choice. If you cannot stop the server, copy at a quiet moment and keep several generations. Test a restore once. Updating Take a backup, stop the server, replace the program files keeping data/ and start again. Database changes are applied automatically. See Installation installation.html . Monitoring The server logs to standard output certificate fingerprints, migrations, warnings and errors. Watch that log with your service manager. A simple health check is requesting the login page. Moving to a new machine Copy data/ to the new machine and start the server there. If the address changes, update publicHost and delete data/certs/ to get a new certificate. Clients that trusted the old certificate will ask again. "},{"slug":"security","title":"Security and privacy","desc":"How MeshCrowd protects accounts and data, what end-to-end encryption covers and where the honest limits are.","group":"Operating a server","headings":[{"id":"what-is-protected-and-how","text":"What is protected, and how","level":2},{"id":"security-center","text":"Security Center","level":2},{"id":"end-to-end-encrypted-dms","text":"End-to-end encrypted DMs","level":2},{"id":"limits-to-know","text":"Limits to know","level":3},{"id":"notes-channels","text":"Notes channels","level":2},{"id":"what-the-operator-can-see","text":"What the operator can see","level":2},{"id":"the-trust-assumption-in-the-web-client","text":"The trust assumption in the web client","level":2},{"id":"passport-and-strengthened-sign-in","text":"Passport and strengthened sign-in","level":2},{"id":"federation","text":"Federation","level":2},{"id":"reporting-a-vulnerability","text":"Reporting a vulnerability","level":2},{"id":"hardening-checklist","text":"Hardening checklist","level":2}],"text":" What is protected, and how Transport HTTPS and WSS everywhere, with a generated certificate or your own. Passwords bcrypt with 12 rounds. For strengthened accounts the server only ever sees a derived key, not the password. Sessions opaque server side tokens in an httpOnly cookie, individually revocable, not JWTs. Two factor TOTP with single use recovery codes. Uploads extension filtered, size capped and served as downloads under a sandboxing Content Security Policy. Headers and limits security headers and a Content Security Policy on every response, and rate limiting on sensitive endpoints. No third parties the web client loads nothing from a CDN, and there is no analytics. Security Center Admin Panel, Security Center site administrators only holds the tools against bots and floods. It all runs on your server; nothing is sent to a third party captcha or reputation service. Captcha a distorted picture on sign in and sign up, shown never, after a number of failed attempts, or always. Pick random characters, dictionary words built in English and Hungarian, or your own list typed into the editor or a simple sum, and tune the distortion. A captcha works once, so a wrong guess needs a new picture. Flood protection an address that sends too many requests, keeps hitting the rate limits or keeps failing to sign in is banned for a while. A burst of such bans turns on under attack mode , which requires a captcha for every sign in and sign up. IP bans addresses, ranges 1.2.3.4 1.2.3.9 and networks 10.0.0.0/8 , IPv4 and IPv6, permanent or timed. You cannot ban your own address. Blocklists subscribe to public lists of known bad addresses Spamhaus DROP, Tor exit nodes, FireHOL or your own URL. Updates run on a schedule and a failed update keeps the old copy. Allowlist addresses that are never banned or limited. This machine itself is on it by default. Bot traps a hidden field and a speed check on the forms , a sign up cap per address , an IP check tool and an event log . If MeshCrowd runs behind a reverse proxy, set trustProxy in config.json ; otherwise every visitor looks like the proxy and the per address limits cannot tell people apart. End to end encrypted DMs Any 1 1 DM between two people on the same server can be switched to end to end encryption with the lock button. It is one way to go back, delete the conversation and start a new one. The server stores only ciphertext. Keys come from each person's Passport. Safety numbers an encrypted DM has a Verify shield showing a 60 digit number both people can compare over a trusted channel. Each device pins the other person's key the first time it talks to them; if that key later changes, sending is blocked until you review and accept it. Pinning and verification are per device. In an encrypted conversation editing, forwarding, polls, voice messages, scheduling and attachments are disabled. Limits to know It works reliably from one device at a time; two devices sending into the same conversation can collide and show \"Unable to decrypt\". It is local only 1 1 between people on the same server. Federated DMs are not encrypted. A new or cleared device cannot read history it never saw. Decrypted history is cached on the device. Notes channels Notes are encrypted in the browser with a key derived from your Passport, so neither the database nor the admins can read them. Losing your Passport means losing your notes. What the operator can see The server operator can read ordinary channel messages and uploads, because the server stores them. End to end encrypted DMs and Notes are the exception. Bots send what they are asked to their AI provider, so choose providers you trust. The trust assumption in the web client Whoever serves the web client is trusted to serve honest JavaScript. A malicious operator could ship code that captures a password or a key. This is true of every web based end to end design. Host your own server, or use a server run by people you trust, and compare certificate fingerprints. Passport and strengthened sign in For web accounts the browser derives two keys from your password authKey is sent and stored as a bcrypt hash, and wrapKey wraps your Passport seed and never leaves the browser. Residual risks authKey acts like a password on that server so TLS is required, and a weak password can be guessed offline from authKey . Failed Passport proofs lock that identity for 15 minutes after five failures. The phone interface asks for your password again before it opens the Admin Panel or Server Settings; that check is rate limited and locks out after repeated wrong answers. Federation Peers are trusted only for identity, permissions are always decided by the owning instance, peers must be approved first, and calls to peers refuse redirects and non public addresses. See Federation federation.html . Reporting a vulnerability Please report security problems privately to the project maintainers rather than in a public issue, and give them a reasonable time to fix them before you publish. Hardening checklist Use a certificate from a real authority and keep it renewed. Behind a proxy set trustProxy to a hop count, never true on an exposed server. Keep Node.js and the server up to date. Restrict who can create Sites and bots, since both can run code or send data outward. Give moderators only the permissions they need and review the audit log. Back up data/ and test restoring it. "},{"slug":"troubleshooting","title":"Troubleshooting and FAQ","desc":"Common problems with certificates, ports, voice, sign-in and notifications, plus known limitations and frequently asked questions.","group":"Operating a server","headings":[{"id":"quick-fixes","text":"Quick fixes","level":2},{"id":"faq","text":"FAQ","level":2},{"id":"known-limitations","text":"Known limitations","level":2}],"text":" Quick fixes Symptom What to check Browser warns about the certificate Expected with the self signed certificate accept it once. For no warning use a certificate from a real authority with serverCrt and serverKey . The warning says the certificate does not match the address publicHost did not match the address you use when the certificate was generated. Fix publicHost , delete data/certs/ and restart. The server exits with certs Your serverCrt or serverKey is missing, invalid, mismatched, too weak, or only one of them is set. The message names the file and the reason. Cannot find module 'node sqlite' Node.js is older than 22.5. Use the bundled runtime or the start scripts. Port already in use Change port or httpsPort in data/config.json . Voice works on the LAN but not across networks Run setup turn.bat or setup turn.sh , or turn on Admin Panel, Calls , then forward UDP and TCP 3478 and UDP 49152 49999 on the router. Press Test in Calls, and try a phone on mobile data. See STUN and TURN configuration.html stun and turn . A red \"Connection lost. Reconnecting...\" banner that never goes away Live updates use a WebSocket. Older servers only accepted it when the page was opened through publicHost , localhost or 127.0.0.1 , so another address a LAN IP, a second name, the Android emulator's 10.0.2.2 was refused with HTTP 403. Update the server; on older ones set publicHost to the address people use. Behind a reverse proxy also forward Host and set trustProxy . No microphone or camera prompt The page is not on HTTPS or localhost. \"Unrecognised server address\" when signing in with a Passport Set publicHost to the address people type, or add the exact origin to passportOrigins . Sign in loops behind a reverse proxy Set trustProxy to the hop count and forward Host and X Forwarded Proto . Cookies not marked Secure behind a proxy Same trustProxy is not set. The Android app says \"invalid credentials\" for a strengthened account Update the app to 3.0 or newer, or use the web client. No notifications on Android Check the battery settings for the app, the notification mode in You, Android app , and that the server is reachable over HTTPS. UnifiedPush does nothing with a ntfy on the LAN Set pushAllowPrivateEndpoints to true on the server. Lines like TLS client error or SSL alert bad certificate in the log Older versions logged every failed TLS handshake. These come from scanners and bots probing the port and are harmless; newer versions stay silent. Set the environment variable MESHCROWD TLS DEBUG=1 to log one line per failed handshake with the client address. If a real user is affected, check that the certificate covers the hostname they use and that serverCrt contains the full chain. \"Unable to decrypt\" in an encrypted DM Two devices wrote into the same conversation, or this device never saw that history. Use one device at a time. A Site shows a PHP error about a missing DLL Run npm run fetch php and use the bundled server, or install the Visual C++ redistributable. FAQ Is it really free? Yes. It is free software under the GNU General Public License and has no paid tiers. Do I need a domain name? Not for a LAN. For people outside your network you want one, plus a real certificate. How many people can it host? It depends on your hardware. Text chat is light. Voice is peer to peer, so the limit for calls is each person's upload bandwidth, not the server. Roughly eight or more people with video in one room strains most home connections. Can I import from another chat service? Not at the moment. Can I run it with Docker? There is no official image yet. It is a single Node.js process, so wrapping it is straightforward. Is there email verification or password reset by email? No. Recovery uses your Passport file, and two factor uses TOTP. Does it phone home? No. There is no telemetry, no analytics and the web client loads nothing from a CDN. Outgoing connections happen only when you configure them AI providers, webhooks, federation, UnifiedPush and the link previews the server fetches for links people post. How do I move to another machine? Copy the data/ folder. See Administration administration.html . Known limitations Calls are a full peer to peer mesh with no media server, so large calls with video are heavy for each participant. Federation supports text channels only on remote servers; federated DMs are not end to end encrypted. End to end encrypted DMs work reliably from one device at a time, carry no attachments and are local to one server. Notes attachments are encrypted per file, but their encryption is not bound to the file id. Bot slash commands work in server channels only. Email verification is not implemented. "}]};
